                <pb facs="0334" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.001G29/10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Innes’s note of
                    November 28 last informing you of the date of the King’s coronation, and
                    inviting a representative of the President of the United States to attend the
                    ceremony, I have the honor, under instruction from His Majesty’s principal
                    secretary of state for foreign affairs, to inform you that the King has decided
                    that the State visits are to commence on Monday the 19th of June next and
                    terminate on Wednesday, the 28th of that month.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Bryce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
